# Unix line endings for every text file, in the repository and in the
# working tree too, whatever core.autocrlf says: one kind of line ending
# everywhere, so tools that write files (cargo release, editors, scripts)
# never leave a file half CRLF and half LF. Binaries are found by git
# itself; the ones below are named to be sure.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sf2 binary
*.mid binary
*.png binary

# Every branch adds its lines under the changelog's Unreleased heading, so
# two branches always clash there: merging keeps both sides' lines instead.
# (A group heading both added shows up twice; src/changelog.rs reads them
# as one.) GitHub's merge button and conflict check ignore this: merge
# master into the branch with git to get it.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
